-- SYNTHETIC ORACLE FUSION PAYROLL TEST DATA
-- 10 rows for each unique table listed in fusion_PAYROLL_CREATE_tables.sql.
-- 35 unique tables x 10 rows = 350 rows.
--
-- IMPORTANT EXECUTION PRE-REQUISITES:
--   1. Run fusion_HR_CREATE_tables.sql and fusion_HR_DATA.sql first.
--   2. Run the payroll CREATE TABLE script before this data script.
--   3. Run this script once on empty payroll tables; reruns will cause PK conflicts.
--
-- HR alignment from the supplied fusion_HR_DATA.sql:
--   PERSON_ID 1001-1010; BUSINESS_GROUP_ID 500; LDG_ID 101-110;
--   ORGANIZATION_ID 201-210; JOB_ID 301-310; GRADE_ID 401-410;
--   POSITION_ID 701-710; LOCATION_ID 601-610.
--   PER_ALL_ASSIGNMENTS_M rows connect each person to their corresponding
--   HR organization, job, grade, position and location.
--
-- Payroll IDs are synthetic and consistent across payroll setup, periods,
-- relationships, assignments, flows, actions, entries, balances and exceptions.
-- The SQL uses no foreign-key constraints and does not re-insert HR master data.
-- Duplicate PAY_PAYROLL_ACTIONS DDL occurrence in the source file is handled once.
--
-- Run order is dependency-friendly. All nullable columns not needed for the
-- demonstration are omitted from INSERT column lists.
--


